          "overall_reasoning": "This is rMATS skipped-exon output with one aligned event (single row), so correlation strategies would not work. Every numeric column is compared with thresholded RAE instead. The columns that matter most for detecting alternative splicing are the junction counts (IJC/SJC), the effective form lengths, the inclusion levels (PSI) and their difference, and the statistics (PValue, FDR).\n- **Junction counts:** RAE with tight tolerances, so small differences from aligner or version changes still pass.\n- **Form lengths:** these are deterministic given read length, so they get a very tight tolerance.\n- **PSI values:** rMATS rounds these to 3 decimals, so they get a moderate tolerance.\n- **IncLevelDifference:** this value is small (-0.023), which makes relative error unstable, so it gets a looser tolerance. Sign is kept because it shows the direction of the effect.\n- **PValue and FDR:** a moderate tolerance allows for differences in numerical optimisation between runs.\n- **ID and ID.1:** these are arbitrary event indices and are ignored.\n- **GeneID and geneSymbol:** these are annotation strings (here, placeholders). They are compared with exact match.",
